// Title: Potential Persistence Via CHM Helper DLL
// Sigma ID: 976dd1f2-a484-45ec-aa1d-0e87e882262b
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-21 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: persistence
// Description: Detects when an attacker modifies the registry key "HtmlHelp Author" to achieve persistence
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://persistence-info.github.io/Data/htmlhelpauthor.html
//   - https://www.hexacorn.com/blog/2018/04/22/beyond-good-ol-run-key-part-76/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_persistence_chm.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "\\Software\\Microsoft\\HtmlHelp Author\\Location" or RegistryKey contains "\\Software\\WOW6432Node\\Microsoft\\HtmlHelp Author\\Location"
